  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically addressed all seven responsibility-chain items: obtained serial BP readings and screened for hypertensive emergency symptoms (RC1), assessed wound and systemic signs (RC2), reconciled medications without overreaching (RC3), acknowledged document unreliability and requested original-paper review (RC4), separated preoperative material from current tasks (RC5), built a concrete follow-up plan with owner/timing (RC6), and obtained family teach-back confirming executability (RC7). No serious or minor in-chain error occurred. The trajectory triggered and actively completed two high-order points—HO3 (dynamic reprioritization when BP spiked to 180/110, then stable windows) and HO4 (safe bounded closure naming residual uncertainty, owner, timing, and emergency triggers)—each with distinct citations and meaningful impact. No important non-chain defect was present, and closure was safe, executable, traceable, and valid. Therefore the grade is 5 (Perfect).",
